# netsurf: boxless child-list changes need no rebuild; late iframes and images built alone (patch 378)
# Generated 2026-11-06
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 377)
#
# The r102 census: "new element is not a plain block, list item or block
# of blocks" (youtube 7, guardian 1). A temporary trace (the element, its
# parent, its descendants' tags) found two shapes:
#   - <head> in <html> (youtube 2, claude, bbc, cnnlite): a script changed
#     <html>'s child list -- typically a <script> appended to it (unit
#     362's shape) -- and the walk read the box-less <head> as new;
#   - <iframe> in <body> (youtube 4, guardian 2, cnnlite 1): ad and
#     tracker frames appended by script.
#
#  - <head> joins 377's never-boxed tags.
#  - html_reconvert_local_childlist(): appendChild / insertBefore /
#    removeChild marks (macos9_reconvert.c) tell the local answer that the
#    node is the parent whose children changed. html_rl_block_change then
#    answers a change on that parent that added or removed no element
#    with a box with no rebuild -- the box tree already matches -- unless
#    structural pseudo-classes or counters are in page CSS (192: a
#    <script> before a <p> takes its :first-child) or a sibling rule can
#    see the skipped elements (198). Removed box-less elements are not
#    known there; only a tag-only sibling rule naming one could see it go.
#  - An <iframe> or <img> appended at the end (no later sibling with a box,
#    no later text) is built alone wherever box_construct puts it -- an
#    inline one at the end of the parent's last line, which is its place
#    exactly then -- and the page laid out whole. A frame gets its record
#    and its late load as in a full build (patch 244). Mid-page ones still
#    take the full rebuild.
#
# Result on a 2500-paragraph sim page: a <script> appended to <html>
# 105 -> 4 ms; an <iframe> appended to <body> 103 -> 30 ms; a pixel <img>
# 105 -> 16 ms.
#
